 See [examples/realtime_client.py](../../examples/realtime_client.py) for a client with the `openai` library.
 
+#### Incremental text input
+
+Text models can use `/v1/realtime?input=text` without an audio encoder. In router mode, also pass the `model` query parameter. `session.created` returns a server-generated `chat_id` (the session ID). One socket owns one slot and chat, including its KV state, across turns. Closing the socket releases it; a chat ID is not a reconnect or authentication token.
+
+After `session.update` sets instructions and `output_modalities: ["text"]`, send complete current user-text hypotheses with increasing revisions:
+
+```json
+{"type":"input_text_buffer.update","revision":1,"text":"Suggest a good b"}
+{"type":"input_text_buffer.update","revision":2,"text":"Suggest a good book"}
+{"type":"input_text_buffer.update","revision":3,"text":"Suggest a fantasy book"}
+```
+
+The server tokenizes text with its own vocabulary. Do not send token IDs from a different model. Updates can extend or correct the open user turn. Revisions must be positive integers below `INT64_MAX`; text is limited to 1 MiB and the model context limit. The server retains the matching token prefix and removes the revised KV suffix. If the memory backend cannot remove a suffix, it clears and replays the known conversation tokens. Generated history stays in context for the next turn.
+
+Each scheduler pass decodes at most one available `n_batch` of pending input before returning to the task queue. The next pass consumes newly arrived revisions and continues immediately if tokens remain. There is no input timer or requirement to wait for a complete word or sentence. At an empty input queue, the slot waits without sampling output.
+
+`input_text_buffer.updated` acknowledges an accepted revision. `input_text_buffer.prefill` reports `chat_id`, `revision`, `batch_tokens`, `total_tokens`, `batch_start_us`, `batch_end_us`, and `finished`. Batch timestamps use the server monotonic clock. A newer hypothesis can supersede an older revision before that older revision finishes prefilling.
+
+When the user's turn is complete, send `response.create`. The server finishes pending prefill, adds the assistant generation prompt, and streams `response.output_text.delta` through `response.done`. Use `response.cancel` and wait for `response.done` before opening a replacement user turn. Instructions cannot change after the conversation starts. This text-only mode currently requires a chat template with derivable role boundaries and no tools.
+
+Text-only sessions advertise `input_speculation: true`. To generate from a provisional prefix, send `{"type":"response.create","response":{"speculative":true}}` after its prefill finishes. Output streams immediately. Send `{"type":"response.discard"}` before revising the prefix: this cancels generation and restores the open user turn, then acknowledges `response.discarded`. A partial prompt checkpoint restores recurrent/SWA state while dense KV is trimmed; unsupported restoration falls back to replaying the known input. Send `{"type":"response.accept"}` to keep the generated response as conversation history. Speculation retains one checkpoint per active slot. Playback policy belongs to the downstream client.
+
 ### POST `/v1/responses`: OpenAI-compatible Responses API
 
